    intro: `The $2 million to $5 million band is where La Quinta's private golf market is deepest and where the buyer has the most genuine choice. Below it, the options narrow to PGA West and the older neighborhoods; above it, to a handful of estate communities. In between, six of the seven clubs have meaningful inventory, and the decision becomes about fit rather than availability. At PGA West, this band covers the better single-family homes and the smaller estate lots on the southern side — larger floor plans, more open views and proximity to the private courses rather than the resort ones. At The Tradition, it covers most of the community: Arnold Palmer's only Coachella Valley design, a walkable routing, and a settled streetscape of traditional Spanish-Mediterranean homes with the most mature landscaping in La Quinta. At Andalusia, it covers a large share of the post-2005 custom homes and the fairway villas, in a community whose defining quality is architectural consistency and a family-oriented membership. At La Quinta Country Club, the band includes the substantial custom remodels around the 1959 course — the only La Quinta club neighborhood within walking distance of Old Town. At The Hideaway, it reaches the fairway homes and some of the more modest custom homes on the Clive Clark side, behind a gate with 36 holes of Dye and Clark golf. At The Quarry, it may reach some of the 1990s and 2000s vintage homes, though inventory there is small in absolute terms and turns slowly. The Madison Club generally sits above this band. Because so many communities overlap here, the useful questions are about lifestyle. How much golf, and what kind — the variety of PGA West's six courses, or the intimacy of a single walkable Palmer routing? How much social calendar — Andalusia's junior programming and events, or Hideaway's morning-golf rhythm? How much scale — a community with resort traffic and a Tour event, or a member-and-guest club with a tight cap? Full-time or seasonal — and if seasonal, how important is walkability to town versus a quiet southern gate? Club economics remain a factor. At this price point the initiation deposit is a smaller share of the total than in the entry band, but transfer terms, refundability and dues still vary meaningfully between clubs, and our Buying Into an Equity Club guide covers what to ask. We do not publish price statistics on this page; the quarterly 92253 Market Report and a licensed California professional are the sources for current numbers. When listings are connected, this page will show inventory priced $2,000,000–$5,000,000 across all seven communities. The Community Quiz is the fastest way to narrow this band to two or three clubs.`,
